00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:25,970
And after I told them about my life,
they told me they were jealous of my dad.

241
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:26,888
<i>Yeah?</i>

242
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:30,225
That he was
so loved and cared for like that.

243
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:31,142
<i>Mmm.</i>

244
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:34,145
They said he was so lucky
to have met a woman like you

245
00:13:34,146 --> 00:13:36,773
and that you were
such an amazing wife and person.

246
00:13:36,774 --> 00:13:37,690
<i>Mmm. Mmm, mmm.</i>

247
00:13:37,691 --> 00:13:40,402
And I had never looked at it
that way before, you know?

248
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:44,782
I'd never thought about it enough
to get there.

249
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,159
<i>Mmm. Yeah.</i>

250
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:52,789
And I think that's because I'd always felt
exactly the opposite about you, Mika.

251
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:54,833
<i>I see. Mmm.</i>

252
00:13:54,834 --> 00:13:57,795
- It took so long to say this, but…
<i>- It's okay.</i>

253
00:13:58,546 --> 00:14:00,088
- I hope we keep--
<i>- You know what?</i>

254
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:03,508
<i>Honestly, just being able
to have this conversation</i>

255
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:04,634
<i>makes me happy.</i>

256
00:14:04,635 --> 00:14:08,264
<i>A few years ago, I never would've thought
this talk could happen for us.</i>

257
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:11,766
Right now,
I feel nothing but appreciation for you.

258
00:14:11,767 --> 00:14:15,061
- I just respect you as a person, so much.
<i>- Aw, thank you.</i>

259
00:14:15,062 --> 00:14:17,355
Working so hard, barely sleeping.

260
00:14:17,356 --> 00:14:20,567
<i>Yeah. No sleep at all.</i>

261
00:14:20,568 --> 00:14:22,485
So I just wanted to say thank you,

262
00:14:22,486 --> 00:14:24,821
- and I'm sorry.
<i>- This has been such a lovely phone call.</i>

263
00:14:24,822 --> 00:14:28,533
<i>I think I'll have sweet dreams tonight.</i>

264
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:30,827
<i>- Thank you.</i>
- I hope you have sweet dreams.

265
00:14:30,828 --> 00:14:33,329
- I know you have a busy day tomorrow.
<i>- Yeah.</i>

266
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:35,499
- Good night.
<i>- Okay. Bye.</i>

267
00:14:51,473 --> 00:14:53,349
Her mom must be so happy.

268
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:55,184
Oh, I'm sure it made her happy.

269
00:14:55,185 --> 00:14:57,770
Especially if they had
a tough relationship for so long.

270
00:14:57,771 --> 00:15:00,899
- And especially since she's her stepmom.
- Yeah.

271
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,109
- They're not related by blood, of course.
- Right.

272
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:05,737
- But despite that, there's this deep bond.
- Mmm-hmm.

273
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:08,698
And the fact
they were able to create this bond

274
00:15:08,699 --> 00:15:12,201
is so heartwarming,
to know they found that with each other.

275
00:15:12,202 --> 00:15:15,413
- Biological ties are important, of course.
- Mmm-hmm.

276
00:15:15,414 --> 00:15:17,916
But it reminds me
that family isn't always about blood.

277
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:21,252
Actually, I have
quite a few stepchildren myself.

278
00:15:21,253 --> 00:15:22,712
- Oh, you do?
- From my late husband.

279
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:24,839
Oh, you do, that's right, of course.

280
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,549
- I have five bonus kids.
- I see.

281
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:27,508
That many?

282
00:15:27,509 --> 00:15:30,053
When they were younger,
they'd give me such a hard time,

283
00:15:30,054 --> 00:15:31,638
and they'd say things like,

284
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:35,516
"My mom and dad will get back together,
so we don't need you at all."

285
00:15:35,517 --> 00:15:36,851
- Really?
- Wow.

286
00:15:36,852 --> 00:15:38,895
But now, we're super close.

287
00:15:38,896 --> 00:15:41,814
- Oh, that's amazing.
- I even brought them to Japan.

288
00:15:41,815 --> 00:15:43,024
- Yeah.
- Great.

289
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:46,069
- So I truly empathized with that.
- Of course.

290
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:49,531
I know that if my stepchildren
ever said something like this to me,

291
00:15:50,449 --> 00:15:52,952
- I would be incredibly happy to hear it.
- Sure.

292
00:15:58,582 --> 00:16:02,210
<i>Today,
the guys will compete against each other</i>

293
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:05,631
<i>to test their mettle
and win an overnight date.</i>

294
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:11,469
<i>You'll compete in the Dead Hang Challenge.</i>

295
00:16:11,470 --> 00:16:12,596
I'm done.

296
00:16:13,597 --> 00:16:14,848
All right.

297
00:16:15,432 --> 00:16:17,642
They look so tense.

298
00:16:17,643 --> 00:16:20,437
This feels totally different
than our tug-of-war.

299
00:16:21,021 --> 00:16:23,982
<i>The last man hanging gets to ask out</i>

300
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:26,860
<i>whichever girl he's interested in now.</i>

301
00:16:29,279 --> 00:16:31,614
- Huh?
- You're not doing it, right?

302
00:16:31,615 --> 00:16:34,450
- Of course I'm not doing it.
- We figured you wouldn't.

303
00:16:34,451 --> 00:16:35,535
I didn't think so.

304
00:16:35,536 --> 00:16:38,037
Because Asuka's not here.

305
00:16:38,038 --> 00:16:42,458
It'd be rude to everyone if I competed.
Besides, I get way too competitive.

306
00:16:42,459 --> 00:16:44,585
So I'm sitting this one out. Make sense?

307
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:46,004
- Yeah, sure.
- All right.

308
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:48,798
- Kazuma, how hungry are you to win?
- I'll do my best.

309
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:49,633
Yep.

310
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:52,301
I'll fight hard.

311
00:16:52,302 --> 00:16:53,344
Good.

312
00:16:53,345 --> 00:16:54,971
I'll be the lone survivor.

313
00:16:54,972 --> 00:16:56,807
Yes!

314
00:16:57,433 --> 00:16:58,976
- And Ari?
- I'll do it.

315
00:16:59,643 --> 00:17:01,644
- He's nervous.
- You worried?

316
00:17:01,645 --> 00:17:03,104
Leo?

317
00:17:03,105 --> 00:17:04,731
Ruru! We're going on a date!

318
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:06,899
- Ooh!
- Good luck!

319
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:09,736
Wait, my hands are sweaty.

320
00:17:09,737 --> 00:17:11,739
- For real?
- Here we go.

321
00:17:12,656 --> 00:17:13,657
Ready?

322
00:17:14,241 --> 00:17:15,242
Go!

323
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:25,669
Ten seconds.

324
00:17:34,636 --> 00:17:35,554
Twenty.

325
00:17:40,684 --> 00:17:41,643
One minute.

326
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:45,897
Hold on, my hands are slipping.

327
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:48,274
What? For real?

328
00:17:48,275 --> 00:17:50,193
- Ah…
- Come on, Tai-chan.

329
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:51,986
<i>Leo!</i>

330
00:17:51,987 --> 00:17:54,573
- One minute ten.
- Ari's doing great.

331
00:17:59,119 --> 00:18:02,163
- <i>Bo looks totally relaxed.</i>
- <i>Bo's still there. Hanging on.</i>

332
00:18:02,164 --> 00:18:03,998
- I'm losing grip.
- <i>Ari's in danger.</i>

333
00:18:03,999 --> 00:18:05,917
- Oh no.
- <i>Oh no, Ari's out.</i>

334
00:18:05,918 --> 00:18:08,128
<i>Ah, who's it gonna be?</i>

335
00:18:09,004 --> 00:18:10,089
Oh, hold on.

336
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:12,006
I can't.

337
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:13,174
<i>Whoa, Kazu-kun!</i>

338
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:15,594
- Ninety seconds.
- He could've gone longer.

339
00:18:16,678 --> 00:18:18,764
Okay, Kazuma's the winner.

340
00:18:21,308 --> 00:18:22,267
Congrats.

341
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:25,437
Who do you choose?

342
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,356
Ruru, let's go.

343
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,233
- Let's do it.
- Right.

344
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:35,029
Kazuma, Ruru, have fun.

345
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,739
- Good luck!
- Have a great time.

346
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:38,826
- We're off.
- Enjoy yourselves.

347
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:43,996
- An overnight trip is huge, yeah?
- It definitely is.

348
00:18:43,997 --> 00:18:47,250
An overnight trip's a big deal. Mmm.

349
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:49,335
He keeps saying that.

350
00:18:49,336 --> 00:18:51,338
Huge deal. Mmm.

351
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:54,049
<i>I totally sucked at that.</i>

352
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:57,093
My hands were sweating. I was nervous.

353
00:18:57,094 --> 00:19:00,430
It was super frustrating.
Also, I wanted anyone but Kazuma to win.

354
00:19:01,014 --> 00:19:02,933
<i>I knew he'd pick Ruru. For sure.</i>

355
00:19:04,685 --> 00:19:07,687
When he picked Ruru,
I was seriously devastated.

356
00:19:07,688 --> 00:19:09,355
Like, "I'm cooked."

357
00:19:09,356 --> 00:19:12,942
I mean, I woke up and got ready
before everyone else

358
00:19:12,943 --> 00:19:15,653
because I thought,
"Oh, I have to pack for tomorrow too."

359
00:19:15,654 --> 00:19:17,989
But it was all for nothing.

360
00:19:17,990 --> 00:19:19,866
- That's cute.
- Adorable.

361
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:21,952
He's so sweet.

362
00:19:22,536 --> 00:19:26,165
I'm going to make sure that Ruru's arrow
points 100% towards me.

363
00:19:27,082 --> 00:19:29,710
I'll share what I feel
so she'll only think about me,

364
00:19:30,419 --> 00:19:31,961
even when we're back.

365
00:19:31,962 --> 00:19:33,005
Mmm.

366
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:36,800
"If you won't sing, I'll make you sing,
my Ruru bird."

367
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:39,469
I hope to deliver on that promise.

368
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:41,847
I will.

369
00:19:43,765 --> 00:19:46,310
Oh, my God. What if we bang?

370
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:49,520
No response?

371
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:50,563
I wish you would.

372
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:51,856
You should just be yourself.

373
00:19:51,857 --> 00:19:55,151
Even if you do it, you could be like,
"Hey, Leo," and it'll be fine.

374
00:19:55,152 --> 00:19:58,779
Sure, it would actually be kind of funny
but also totally shitty of me.

375
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:00,865
I mean, yeah, I guess you're right.

376
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:04,285
- Because it'll be like you cheated on him.
- Yeah, yeah, for sure.

377
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:06,787
- That would gross him out.
- But Leo knows that.

378
00:20:06,788 --> 00:20:09,123
If he accepts you after that,
then he's a man, for sure.

379
00:20:09,124 --> 00:20:10,875
But you saw Leo's face, right?

380
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:14,170
Even though you aren't dating yet,
he looked heartbroken.

381
00:20:14,171 --> 00:20:15,380
- <i>Yeah.</i>
- <i>True.</i>

382
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:19,509
<i>Of course that's how he is.</i>

383
00:20:20,260 --> 00:20:22,970
<i>Because he promised her
he'd take her out on a date.</i>

384
00:20:22,971 --> 00:20:25,681
You know,
that suitcase is packed to the brim.

385
00:20:25,682 --> 00:20:28,393
I overthink things a lot.
I put a ton of stuff in it.

386
00:20:30,187 --> 00:20:31,646
- Ruru!
- Gosh.

387
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:33,731
- Zuma!
- You scared me.

388
00:20:33,732 --> 00:20:35,233
- You can't come.
- What?

389
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:38,069
Shut up. Let me just give her this.

390
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:39,987
- Wait, what's that?
- It's my necklace.

391
00:20:39,988 --> 00:20:41,072
- What?
- <i>Wow.</i>

392
00:20:41,073 --> 00:20:42,907
- Kazuma. No sexy time.
- Hmm?

393
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:45,117
- We won't be doing sexy time.
- Be good, okay?

394
00:20:45,118 --> 00:20:48,037
We won't.
It'd be wild if she thinks we would.

395
00:20:48,038 --> 00:20:50,331
- For sure.
- You gonna go buck wild?

396
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:53,042
Okay, I'll stop. Yeah?

397
00:20:53,043 --> 00:20:54,293
Is it on?

398
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:56,128
I messed up and put it on wrong.

399
00:20:56,129 --> 00:20:57,964
He's not the smooth type.

400
00:20:57,965 --> 00:20:59,967
What's that?

401
00:21:00,759 --> 00:21:03,428
My mind's a mess right know.

402
00:21:04,012 --> 00:21:04,929
- I'm off.
- See ya.

403
00:21:04,930 --> 00:21:06,430
- Bye-bye.
- Hmm.

404
00:21:06,431 --> 00:21:08,015
Kazuma, you understand?

405
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:10,101
No sexy stuff.

406
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:11,852
- Don't do it.
- I said we won't. Go inside.

407
00:21:11,853 --> 00:21:13,272
I'll beat you up.

408
00:21:13,855 --> 00:21:15,731
They're gonna do it.

409
00:21:15,732 --> 00:21:18,859
- They'll find the camera's blind spots.
- They will, right? Yeah, somehow.

410
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:21,238
- They seem like they'd do it covertly.
- They'll be sneaky.

411
00:21:22,197 --> 00:21:23,991
- Did you see her off?
- Yeah.

412
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:27,034
Do you want to borrow my chest
to cry on today?

413
00:21:27,035 --> 00:21:29,537
- You can lean on me too.
- It's okay to cry.

414
00:21:29,538 --> 00:21:31,456
I'm fine. I trust her.

415
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:33,542
- Yeah.
- We know.

416
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:36,044
For sure. We know that.

417
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:38,546
- Thinking about it won't help.
- Yeah.

418
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:40,798
No point in dwelling on something
you can't control.

419
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:43,302
- True. That'll only bring me down.
- Exactly.

420
00:21:45,721 --> 00:21:50,266
<i>Those remaining in school
will help out the local community.</i>

421
00:21:50,267 --> 00:21:55,438
<i>The beaches of Okinawa
are littered with large amounts of debris.</i>

422
00:21:55,439 --> 00:21:58,858
<i>You'll be working together
to clean up the beach.</i>

423
00:21:58,859 --> 00:22:01,027
- Off-campus bonding?
- We're picking up litter?

424
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:02,153
- Cleaning the beach.
- Yeah.

425
00:22:02,154 --> 00:22:04,864
Let's pick up trash. I see some.

426
00:22:04,865 --> 00:22:06,532
Let's do this!

427
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:07,742
I'm so ready for this.

428
00:22:07,743 --> 00:22:09,493
- I'm committed.
- It's so dirty.

429
00:22:09,494 --> 00:22:12,288
- Yeah, it's filthy.
- There's so much trash.

430
00:22:12,289 --> 00:22:15,166
- What the heck?
- It's covered in it.

431
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:17,626
- There's some here.
- So much of it.

432
00:22:17,627 --> 00:22:18,628
This is insane.

433
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:21,922
- You've never done this, have you?
- Take this.

434
00:22:21,923 --> 00:22:24,176
Look! I found a huge pile over here.

435
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:27,387
It won't fit.

436
00:22:29,056 --> 00:22:30,682
My bag's already full.

437
00:22:34,144 --> 00:22:36,062
<i>Leo's quietly working as usual.</i>

438
00:22:36,063 --> 00:22:38,440
- <i>Puts his heart into everything.</i>
- <i>Yeah.</i>

439
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,401
<i>So beautiful.</i>

440
00:22:42,402 --> 00:22:44,278
<i>The ocean in Okinawa's so beautiful.</i>

441
00:22:44,279 --> 00:22:45,447
<i>It's so gorgeous.</i>

442
00:22:46,865 --> 00:22:47,824
This is it.

443
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:55,206
Wait, what? Hold up.

444
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:57,041
- What?
- This is insane.

445
00:22:57,042 --> 00:22:59,752
- Amazing! Whoa!
- It's crazy!

446
00:22:59,753 --> 00:23:01,837
Seriously? Wait, is this for real?

447
00:23:01,838 --> 00:23:04,590
- It's incredible!
- Look, there's a pool.

448
00:23:04,591 --> 00:23:07,009
- This is unreal.
- It's deep.

449
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:09,720
It's the perfect temperature,
like a heated pool.

450
00:23:09,721 --> 00:23:11,431
- Wow, amazing!
- Whoa.

451
00:23:12,057 --> 00:23:14,892
- This is getting me hyped up.
- Me too. Go upstairs?

452
00:23:14,893 --> 00:23:15,769
Sure.

453
00:23:17,479 --> 00:23:18,814
Whoa.

454
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:24,068
Look at that!
This is twice as good as I imagined.

455
00:23:24,069 --> 00:23:25,444
Amazing.

456
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:28,864
Where's everyone else?
Maybe they're somewhere over there?

457
00:23:28,865 --> 00:23:31,368
- Yeah, because we crossed that bridge.
- Yeah.

458
00:23:32,953 --> 00:23:35,121
It's heavy.

459
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:36,164
You know?

460
00:23:43,922 --> 00:23:45,424
- Looks deep, doesn't it?
- Yeah.

461
00:23:46,007 --> 00:23:47,509
- It feels so good.
- It's cold.

462
00:23:48,135 --> 00:23:50,387
- It feels super nice.
- This is great.

463
00:23:51,847 --> 00:23:53,973
- It's breathtaking.
- Yeah.

464
00:23:53,974 --> 00:23:54,850
Truly.

465
00:23:56,017 --> 00:23:58,811
- Do you have an ideal in mind?
- An ideal what?

466
00:23:58,812 --> 00:24:01,897
Like, an idea of what
the perfect boyfriend might be like.

467
00:24:01,898 --> 00:24:04,483
- I like somebody who can make me laugh.
- I see.

468
00:24:04,484 --> 00:24:07,403
Every one of my past boyfriends
were pretty funny.

469
00:24:07,404 --> 00:24:09,488
- Hmm.
- Yeah, they all were.

470
00:24:09,489 --> 00:24:13,200
On top of that, we were comfortable
acting like kids when we'd hang out.

471
00:24:13,201 --> 00:24:15,287
That's actually super important to me.

472
00:24:17,330 --> 00:24:20,791
Well, this trip feels like
it's kind of do-or-die.

473
00:24:20,792 --> 00:24:22,126
- Do-or-die?
- Yeah.

474
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:25,046
I mean, it feels like that for me.

475
00:24:28,216 --> 00:24:30,384
I've been wanting to tell you how I feel.

476
00:24:30,385 --> 00:24:31,969
- That's why I invited you.
- Right.

477
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:34,889
At this point,
you're the only one I'm interested in.

478
00:24:34,890 --> 00:24:37,266
So you have no intention
of considering anyone else.

479
00:24:37,267 --> 00:24:40,853
Right. And so,
I want to make a strong impression on you.

480
00:24:40,854 --> 00:24:42,062
Mmm. Yeah.

481
00:24:42,063 --> 00:24:44,231
- While we're on this trip.
- Mmm.

482
00:24:44,232 --> 00:24:46,818
- In two days.
- That makes sense.

483
00:24:49,279 --> 00:24:50,779
- That it?
- All done.

484
00:24:50,780 --> 00:24:52,407
- Looks clean.
- Looks good.

485
00:24:54,826 --> 00:24:56,203
We have to leave them here.

486
00:24:58,622 --> 00:25:01,040
- This seems like a lot of litter, right?
- Yeah.

487
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:03,375
- We picked up a lot.
- I feel like we did a great job.

488
00:25:03,376 --> 00:25:05,753
- Way more than expected.
- Nice work, everyone.

489
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:07,213
Let's make a pile.

490
00:25:07,214 --> 00:25:08,298
- Ha-chan.
- Yeah, okay.

491
00:25:09,341 --> 00:25:11,717
Wait, let me make a spot for it.

492
00:25:11,718 --> 00:25:13,094
It feels amazing!

493
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:23,521
I want to play catch.

494
00:25:23,522 --> 00:25:25,356
- Let's go there.
- Okay.

495
00:25:25,357 --> 00:25:28,193
<i>Tai-chan has such a gentle way
of speaking, doesn't he?</i>

496
00:25:28,944 --> 00:25:30,819
You're good.

497
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:31,780
- Ready? Catch.
- Yeah.

498
00:25:32,489 --> 00:25:34,198
- Got it.
- Good catch.

499
00:25:34,199 --> 00:25:35,825
I try to catch it with my bare hand.

500
00:25:36,409 --> 00:25:38,787
- Yeah, that's a good approach.
- So I'm doing it right?

501
00:25:39,496 --> 00:25:42,414
It's your crush's heart.

502
00:25:42,415 --> 00:25:44,208
- I think I can catch that.
- Yeah.

503
00:25:44,209 --> 00:25:46,835
I'm wondering where my heart is headed.

504
00:25:46,836 --> 00:25:48,837
- Wait, you don't know yet, right?
- No.

505
00:25:48,838 --> 00:25:50,465
Then I'll come and capture it, maybe.

506
00:25:51,341 --> 00:25:53,426
- Oh, really?
- Oh, really?

507
00:25:54,511 --> 00:25:56,428
- "Oh, really?"
- <i>This is nice.</i>

508
00:25:56,429 --> 00:25:57,930
- That was close.
- I made up my mind.

509
00:25:57,931 --> 00:25:59,557
- <i>Oh?</i>
- You did?

510
00:25:59,558 --> 00:26:01,058
- Yep, sure did.
- About what?

511
00:26:01,059 --> 00:26:03,727
Well, I'm going to make a move on you.

512
00:26:03,728 --> 00:26:05,354
- Wait, on me?
- Yes, you!

513
00:26:05,355 --> 00:26:08,774
I'm pining for the same person
that I liked at the beginning.

514
00:26:08,775 --> 00:26:10,652
- Wow, for real?
- No! Yeah.

515
00:26:11,653 --> 00:26:12,487
That's right.

516
00:26:14,281 --> 00:26:16,032
It's like…

517
00:26:16,741 --> 00:26:17,576
What?

518
00:26:19,619 --> 00:26:22,664
It's like what?
I can't catch, I'm flustered.

519
00:26:25,041 --> 00:26:27,085
- You were saying?
- My head is spinning.

520
00:26:29,045 --> 00:26:30,380
- Then, let it spin.
- Yeah.

521
00:26:31,798 --> 00:26:33,091
That's natural.

522
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:37,553
<i>Leo must be dealing
with some complicated feelings.</i>

523
00:26:37,554 --> 00:26:39,179
<i>You're right about that.</i>

524
00:26:39,180 --> 00:26:40,807
- <i>Jian.</i>
- Clink.

525
00:26:41,850 --> 00:26:43,685
"Clink."

526
00:26:45,103 --> 00:26:46,770
Sorry.

527
00:26:46,771 --> 00:26:48,315
Did that surprise you?

528
00:26:52,068 --> 00:26:53,861
Have you had acai?

529
00:26:53,862 --> 00:26:55,988
I used to eat it every day at Bondi Cafe.

530
00:26:55,989 --> 00:26:57,656
Really? Is it good?

531
00:26:57,657 --> 00:26:59,492
- Yeah. It's perfect.
- Yeah.

532
00:27:00,827 --> 00:27:03,370
How old were you when you became a host?

533
00:27:03,371 --> 00:27:05,122
- I was 19.
- 19?

534
00:27:05,123 --> 00:27:07,124
- That's when I started.
- And then--

535
00:27:07,125 --> 00:27:09,461
I moved to Tokyo when I was about 16.

536
00:27:10,045 --> 00:27:11,879
Why did you move so young?

537
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:14,798
- What made you leave?
- Outside the city, there's a hierarchy.

538
00:27:14,799 --> 00:27:17,051
- Yeah.
- It was out of control.

539
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:18,927
The more rural the area,
the worse it gets.

540
00:27:18,928 --> 00:27:20,095
I get that, for sure.

541
00:27:20,096 --> 00:27:22,222
No matter how successful you become…

542
00:27:22,223 --> 00:27:23,140
Mmm.

543
00:27:23,141 --> 00:27:26,144
…you'll always be lower
than people barely older than you.

544
00:27:27,395 --> 00:27:28,812
I got pretty sick of that.

545
00:27:28,813 --> 00:27:31,774
I felt like I couldn't reach
my full potential if I stayed there.

546
00:27:31,775 --> 00:27:32,858
Mmm.

547
00:27:32,859 --> 00:27:33,693
And I thought,

548
00:27:34,611 --> 00:27:37,529
I was always pretty good
at adapting to new environments.

549
00:27:37,530 --> 00:27:39,657
- Mmm.
- I changed schools a lot when I was young.

550
00:27:39,658 --> 00:27:41,158
- Oh, you did?
- Yeah.

551
00:27:41,159 --> 00:27:42,701
- Because of family?
- That's right.

552
00:27:42,702 --> 00:27:43,619
Oh, wow.

553
00:27:43,620 --> 00:27:45,663
I was sent to live
with different relatives,

554
00:27:45,664 --> 00:27:47,831
- so I kept having to switch schools.
- Makes sense.

555
00:27:47,832 --> 00:27:50,584
I thought I could manage on my own,
so I just left.

556
00:27:50,585 --> 00:27:55,297
My mom was in Kanagawa after her divorce,
so, at first, I lived in Kanagawa

557
00:27:55,298 --> 00:27:57,049
- and worked outdoor jobs.
- Mmm.

558
00:27:57,050 --> 00:27:57,926
And then,

559
00:27:58,802 --> 00:28:01,095
I'd go to Shibuya after work.

560
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:04,014
<i>Gyaru-o</i> culture
was prevalent there at the time.

561
00:28:04,015 --> 00:28:06,100
I'd just ask <i>gyaru-os</i> to be my friend.

562
00:28:06,101 --> 00:28:07,101
- Really?
- Yeah.

563
00:28:07,102 --> 00:28:09,770
- I didn't know you were that outgoing.
- Yeah.

564
00:28:09,771 --> 00:28:12,231
So I started making
more and more friends that way.

565
00:28:12,232 --> 00:28:13,148
I see.

566
00:28:13,149 --> 00:28:16,568
And then,
uh, Harajuku style became popular.

567
00:28:16,569 --> 00:28:18,028
- Yeah.
- People were more interested

568
00:28:18,029 --> 00:28:19,947
- in the smart model type.
- Mmm.

569
00:28:19,948 --> 00:28:21,282
- Not the <i>gyaru-o.</i>
- Mmm.

570
00:28:21,950 --> 00:28:24,952
We couldn't keep up with that,
so we hung out in Kabukicho.

571
00:28:24,953 --> 00:28:27,454
That's how I started working as a host
at about 18 or 19.

572
00:28:27,455 --> 00:28:30,791
Oh, I see. So you were a total <i>gyaru-o.</i>

573
00:28:30,792 --> 00:28:32,751
- I ran with a <i>gyaru</i> crew.
- Oh.

574
00:28:32,752 --> 00:28:35,045
- You had long hair and all that?
- Mmm.

575
00:28:35,046 --> 00:28:38,298
- That sounds so Heisei.
- Yeah, super Heisei.

576
00:28:38,299 --> 00:28:41,469
Oh, I'm jealous. Shibuya in the Heisei era
must have been fun.

577
00:28:42,053 --> 00:28:43,178
It was fun.

578
00:28:43,179 --> 00:28:45,723
- And you've been there ever since?
- Yeah.

579
00:28:45,724 --> 00:28:46,807
- Wow.
- Crazy, right?

580
00:28:46,808 --> 00:28:48,142
Yeah.

581
00:28:48,143 --> 00:28:50,186
I love shrimp. This is delicious.

582
00:28:50,854 --> 00:28:51,938
What's your favorite?

583
00:28:52,814 --> 00:28:54,566
- Food, I mean.
- Eggplant.

584
00:28:55,316 --> 00:28:56,525
- Did you say eggplant?
- Mmm.

585
00:28:56,526 --> 00:28:57,526
- Really?
- Yeah.

586
00:28:57,527 --> 00:28:59,111
- That's your favorite food?
- Yeah.

587
00:28:59,112 --> 00:29:01,823
Eggplant is kind of
an unexpected choice, isn't it?

588
00:29:02,407 --> 00:29:03,241
Well…

589
00:29:05,118 --> 00:29:07,161
the one dish I remember
my mom making for me

590
00:29:07,162 --> 00:29:09,455
was eggplant stir-fry with miso sauce.

591
00:29:09,456 --> 00:29:11,623
- Oh, sounds delicious.
- Mmm.

592
00:29:11,624 --> 00:29:14,376
- That's why I've always liked eggplant.
- That makes sense.

593
00:29:14,377 --> 00:29:15,419
- Yeah.
- Okay.

594
00:29:15,420 --> 00:29:18,756
So, it's not about
how good the eggplant tastes.

595
00:29:18,757 --> 00:29:21,968
- It's more about the memory.
- So, yeah, it's about the memory.

596
00:29:23,344 --> 00:29:25,679
I'd been in a single-parent household
since I was little.

597
00:29:25,680 --> 00:29:28,098
And then, when I was in second grade,

598
00:29:28,099 --> 00:29:31,310
my mom ran off with her new husband.

599
00:29:31,311 --> 00:29:34,188
She just left me behind,
and my dad came to pick me up.

600
00:29:34,189 --> 00:29:35,939
But he was very abusive.

601
00:29:35,940 --> 00:29:37,859
After that, I was sent to…

602
00:29:38,735 --> 00:29:39,902
…live with relatives.

603
00:29:39,903 --> 00:29:41,695
They looked after me for a year or two.

604
00:29:41,696 --> 00:29:45,700
I graduated middle school…
and since then, I've been on my own.

605
00:29:46,659 --> 00:29:50,329
To my mom, I'd say things like,
"You abandoned me,"

606
00:29:50,330 --> 00:29:52,831
or "Don't try to act like
you're my mom now."

607
00:29:52,832 --> 00:29:55,043
I would just blurt it out.

608
00:29:56,961 --> 00:29:58,670
But when my mom started crying,

609
00:29:58,671 --> 00:30:01,507
I was like,
"Oh, man, I didn't have to say that."

610
00:30:01,508 --> 00:30:02,967
<i>Now I try to do better.</i>

611
00:30:04,177 --> 00:30:06,721
<i>I try not to badmouth my parents
if I can help it.</i>

612
00:30:08,139 --> 00:30:10,849
<i>Getting to know a person's past
is super important.</i>

613
00:30:10,850 --> 00:30:15,437
I realized people are more than just
what they seem on the outside.

614
00:30:15,438 --> 00:30:17,981
<i>I thought, "He's carried a heavy burden."</i>

615
00:30:17,982 --> 00:30:21,152
<i>"He's lived on his own
and worked hard to get this far in life."</i>

616
00:30:22,070 --> 00:30:24,905
- She has something against host workers.
- Mmm.

617
00:30:24,906 --> 00:30:26,448
He's never opened up like this.

618
00:30:26,449 --> 00:30:28,618
- No, not like this.
- Like, properly shared.

619
00:30:33,414 --> 00:30:36,292
I didn't realize
it'd be so boring without my crush.

620
00:30:37,126 --> 00:30:39,712
- This is no fun at all.
- Yeah, it's boring.

621
00:30:42,215 --> 00:30:43,424
This is great.

622
00:30:44,634 --> 00:30:45,551
So fun!

623
00:30:45,552 --> 00:30:47,678
They're like a rehab group.

624
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:49,638
- Technically, I guess they are.
- That's right.

625
00:30:49,639 --> 00:30:51,682
They're here to rehabilitate
and find love.

626
00:30:51,683 --> 00:30:52,642
Exactly.

627
00:30:56,938 --> 00:30:59,690
Oh, wait. These look delicious!

628
00:30:59,691 --> 00:31:02,776
- This is pretty fancy.
- Incredible. Wow, I love shrimp.

629
00:31:02,777 --> 00:31:05,530
- This is amazing.
- "I love shrimp."

630
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:09,325
Are you still interested in marriage,
after trying it already?

631
00:31:10,118 --> 00:31:11,577
- I am, yeah.
- Oh, you are?

632
00:31:11,578 --> 00:31:12,870
Yeah. I want kids.

633
00:31:12,871 --> 00:31:13,830
I see.

634
00:31:15,206 --> 00:31:16,624
But not necessarily right away.

635
00:31:17,792 --> 00:31:19,711
- Like, you don't want to rush it?
- Mmm.

636
00:31:20,295 --> 00:31:22,046
I want to date someone

637
00:31:23,214 --> 00:31:24,631
properly, for a while.

638
00:31:24,632 --> 00:31:26,967
You like relationships that are long term?

639
00:31:26,968 --> 00:31:29,052
I've almost never been in a relationship.

640
00:31:29,053 --> 00:31:30,679
- Because you were a host, right?
- Mmm.

641
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:32,264
- I see.
- Mmm.

642
00:31:32,265 --> 00:31:33,599
Do you like to take your time

643
00:31:33,600 --> 00:31:35,809
before getting serious
with a relationship?

644
00:31:35,810 --> 00:31:37,436
Or do you ever just dive in?

645
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:38,896
No, I never do that.

646
00:31:38,897 --> 00:31:42,399
- Usually, I know them already.
- Oh, you're already close?

647
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:45,277
- I've only dated people I was close with.
- I see.

648
00:31:45,278 --> 00:31:48,322
We already knew each other
from being in the same friend group.

649
00:31:48,323 --> 00:31:50,949
So I didn't have
to get to know him from scratch.

650
00:31:50,950 --> 00:31:52,743
- We had a foundation.
- You knew them.

651
00:31:52,744 --> 00:31:54,494
- And the chemistry came after.
- Right.

652
00:31:54,495 --> 00:31:57,289
- That's how it's always started for me.
- Okay.

653
00:31:57,290 --> 00:32:01,752
This school is the first time
I'm experiencing the romantic part first.

654
00:32:01,753 --> 00:32:03,837
That's got to be pretty difficult, yeah?

655
00:32:03,838 --> 00:32:05,173
It is, for sure.

656
00:32:21,105 --> 00:32:23,191
This water temperature is perfect.

657
00:32:30,573 --> 00:32:33,159
So you don't like girls
who are bad drunks?

658
00:32:33,993 --> 00:32:37,496
It's fine if they just get happy.
Otherwise, it's a drag.

659
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:39,039
Like, if they get rowdy?

660
00:32:39,040 --> 00:32:40,375
I get rowdy when I drink.

661
00:32:40,959 --> 00:32:44,378
- I'm not a good drunk, to be honest.
- I'm not either, so it's fine.

662
00:32:44,379 --> 00:32:48,090
But even when you're drunk,
you still behave like an adult, right?

663
00:32:48,091 --> 00:32:51,593
No, I get pretty childish.
I was told I'm kind of a baby.

664
00:32:51,594 --> 00:32:54,263
Oh, you mentioned that.
I don't know if I can handle that.

665
00:32:56,140 --> 00:32:58,475
What does "acting like a baby"
look like? Tell me.

666
00:32:58,476 --> 00:33:01,311
- I'm super selfish.
- I want to see you act like a baby.

667
00:33:01,312 --> 00:33:04,690
Wait, I like people who trigger
my maternal instincts, you know?

668
00:33:04,691 --> 00:33:06,275
You could bring that out in me.

669
00:33:07,193 --> 00:33:10,863
If you got childish and clingy with me,
I'd be like, "Oh."

670
00:33:12,699 --> 00:33:14,741
"Maybe I like him." I might think that.

671
00:33:14,742 --> 00:33:16,660
Yeah? "Maybe I like him"?

672
00:33:16,661 --> 00:33:19,329
I can't be clingy when you're wearing
another guy's necklace.

673
00:33:19,330 --> 00:33:21,498
No way I could do that.

674
00:33:21,499 --> 00:33:24,084
- <i>Still thinking about that?</i>
- <i>Of course.</i>

675
00:33:24,085 --> 00:33:25,669
<i>Tell me how you really feel.</i>

676
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:26,713
- <i>Right now?
- Yeah.</i>

677
00:33:27,296 --> 00:33:29,506
You're wearing another guy's necklace

678
00:33:29,507 --> 00:33:31,467
but telling me to be clingy with you.

679
00:33:32,051 --> 00:33:34,386
I'm just saying
I'm curious to see that side of you.

680
00:33:34,387 --> 00:33:36,304
- You don't have to test me.
- I'm not.

681
00:33:36,305 --> 00:33:37,306
- It's how I feel.
- Yeah?

682
00:33:38,641 --> 00:33:40,268
Then take off the necklace.

683
00:33:46,024 --> 00:33:48,692
Oh, this? I keep forgetting about it.

684
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:50,152
- How's that possible?
- Take it off.

685
00:33:50,153 --> 00:33:52,447
I wonder how he'd react
if I was wearing it.

686
00:33:54,157 --> 00:33:57,242
- Would that be rubbing it in?
- Mmm, let's not.

687
00:33:57,243 --> 00:33:58,953
That would probably spark a fight.

688
00:33:59,620 --> 00:34:01,664
- So let's not do that.
- Okay.

689
00:34:04,459 --> 00:34:07,294
- You don't like it?
- Of course not.

690
00:34:07,295 --> 00:34:09,463
- You hate it.
- It doesn't feel good, no.

691
00:34:09,464 --> 00:34:10,505
I see.

692
00:34:10,506 --> 00:34:11,507
Put it on me.

693
00:34:12,341 --> 00:34:14,134
- I'll return it to Leo myself.
- This?

694
00:34:14,135 --> 00:34:15,552
You shouldn't do that.

695
00:34:15,553 --> 00:34:17,637
- Seriously, you shouldn't.
- Why not?

696
00:34:17,638 --> 00:34:19,347
- That would start a fight.
- Yeah?

697
00:34:19,348 --> 00:34:21,933
If you're okay with a fight,
I'll put it on you.

698
00:34:21,934 --> 00:34:23,852
- You're fine with that?
- No, because-- Sure.

699
00:34:23,853 --> 00:34:27,273
It'll definitely cause problems
when we get back. You're good with that?

700
00:34:27,815 --> 00:34:29,192
Let me torture him.

701
00:34:31,027 --> 00:34:31,944
I don't care.

702
00:34:35,573 --> 00:34:38,575
Wait, am I feeling attached
to him right now?

703
00:34:38,576 --> 00:34:41,579
What is this? I don't understand
what I'm feeling about Leo right now.

704
00:34:42,246 --> 00:34:44,956
You know, I think it just feels a little…

705
00:34:44,957 --> 00:34:46,167
- Like what?
- …difficult.

706
00:34:47,585 --> 00:34:50,463
- Because I'm just…
- Then I can't act childish for you.

707
00:34:51,380 --> 00:34:53,924
Come here.

708
00:34:53,925 --> 00:34:55,635
<i>Oh, look!</i>

709
00:34:59,931 --> 00:35:01,682
Your hair smells nice.

710
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:03,434
<i>What?</i>

711
00:35:04,727 --> 00:35:06,187
All I can do is trust.

712
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:08,439
I trust her.

713
00:35:09,732 --> 00:35:11,817
Because I poured my heart out to her.

714
00:35:11,818 --> 00:35:14,153
<i>Watching both sides is killing me.</i>

715
00:35:15,238 --> 00:35:16,571
- How's this?
- Good.

716
00:35:16,572 --> 00:35:19,742
- Oh, they're so lovey-dovey!
- Stop going back and forth!

717
00:35:20,785 --> 00:35:21,619
Okay.

718
00:35:25,540 --> 00:35:29,960
It's not over yet, but I feel like
it's already been a pretty great trip.

719
00:35:29,961 --> 00:35:31,128
I think so too

720
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:34,214
because I was able to open up
about how I feel about you.

721
00:35:34,215 --> 00:35:35,842
The ball is in your court now.

722
00:35:38,261 --> 00:35:40,637
<i>What's she doing?</i>

723
00:35:40,638 --> 00:35:43,014
Isn't it crazy
I kept forgetting about the necklace?

724
00:35:43,015 --> 00:35:43,933
Not at all.

725
00:35:45,685 --> 00:35:48,396
<i>Whoa!</i>

726
00:35:53,192 --> 00:35:54,442
- No.
- This is huge!

727
00:35:54,443 --> 00:35:56,612
- The make out.
- They're making out!

728
00:35:58,114 --> 00:36:00,366
<i>Hey, stop cutting back to him!</i>

729
00:36:03,536 --> 00:36:05,287
Come on, what was that?

730
00:36:05,288 --> 00:36:06,496
A make-out session.

731
00:36:06,497 --> 00:36:08,290
Who was that guy with the moody lighting?

732
00:36:08,291 --> 00:36:09,749
